# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT MUST NEVER LEAVE THIS COMPUTER
#
# The files below contain live passwords. If they reach a public GitHub repo,
# treat every credential in them as compromised and change it: GitHub keeps
# deleted commits reachable for a long time, so removing a file later is not
# the same as it never having been there.
#
# Note for editing this file: a "#" only starts a comment at the START of a
# line. Putting one after a pattern makes it part of the pattern, and the file
# you meant to hide gets committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your admin panel password, in plain text.
ADMIN-LOGIN.txt

# The setup transcript — it prints the admin password too.
setup-log.txt

# Database credentials, application key, admin password.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
debug.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DOWNLOADED, NOT WRITTEN
# Anyone cloning this rebuilds them with one command, and together they are
# hundreds of megabytes of noise in every diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
vendor/
composer.phar

# Build output — regenerated by `npm run build`.
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LARAVEL RUNTIME STATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backend-app/storage/*.key
backend-app/storage/framework/cache/*
backend-app/storage/framework/sessions/*
backend-app/storage/framework/views/*
backend-app/storage/logs/*
backend-app/bootstrap/cache/*
backend-app/public/storage
backend-app/database/*.sqlite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARCHIVES, SCRATCH COPIES, EDITOR AND OS CLUTTER
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.rar
web-development-site/
Claude outputs/

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.local

# Vercel's own link file — machine-specific.
.vercel
